2 CONT
2 CONT CARL HAAKON FEILBERG 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peacefully at his home on his 98th birthday, October 27, 2003, Carl Haakon Feilberg passed away. He is lovingly remembered by his wife Lena (Marquart) of 71 years; his children, Dorwin (Doris) and Carl (Lorna) grandchildren, Heath
2 CONC er (Dean) Mcdonald, Eric (Julie), Erin (Leanne), Lars (Valerie), Caroline, Victoria, Julianna and Kimberly; great-grandchildren, Tanner, Reed, Chelsea, Chloe, Justin, Brendan, Lauren, Riley, Kynan, Arius, Christopher and many niec
2 CONC es and nephews in Canada and Denmark. Haakon was predeceased by parents, Julie and Ditlev; sisters, Eva (Paul) Morch, Anna (Ais) Viggo Pedersen, Elisabeth (Peter) Sundquist, Marie (George) LaCour; brothers, Henning, Niels Peter, N
2 CONC ikolai (Esther). A memorial service will be held October 31 at 2:00 p.m. at Loewen Funeral Chapel in Steinbach with reception to follow. Interment will take place at a later date. A special thanks for the care provided by his home
2 CONC  care workers: Jeannette, Donna, Julie, Bonnie and all the staff at the Seine River Medical Centre, especially Dr. Gobeil and Dr. Doyle. Donations may be made to the North Eastman Health Association, Box 1690, Beausejour, MB R0E 0
2 CONC C0. Arrangements entrusted to: LOEWEN Funeral Chapel 5 Chrysler Gate - Steinbach - 326-1351
2 CONT
2 CONT As published in the Winnipeg Free Press on October 30, 2003
