1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Arne Sørensen (2 October 1906 – 1 March 1978) was a Danish politician, author and resistance fighter. He created the Danish Unity party and became a minister after the occupation. He was an active resistance fighter in the Holger 
2 CONC Danske group under the German occupation and, in 1943, became a key member of the Danish Freedom Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arne_S%C3%B8rensen_(politician)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gravsted.dk/person.php?navn=arnesoerensen
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo: Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0 International license, https://commons.m.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arne_Sorensen.jpg#mw-jump-to-license
