1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The following auto-biographical material is taken from a photo-copy of an original document prepared in 1888 by MICHAEL KJELDSEN in Danish on the occasion of his induction into THE ORDER OF DANNEBROG. This translat
2 CONC ion was executed by Vagn de Leschzky Faurschou and I am most grateful to him for his assistance.
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " I was born in the Manor House Lerkenfeldt in Vesterbolle Parish, Viborg County, on July 23, 1832. My parents were the owners of this manor. My father's name was MATHIAS KJELDSEN and my Mother was METTE KJELDSEN (nee: FAURSCH
2 CONC OU).
2 CONT
2 CONT After being taught by a private tutor in my home, in 1845 I entered high school in Aarhus, Denmark and remained at that school until 1850. In 1851, I was sponsored by Schoolmaster Brix and sent to university. In 1857 I graduated a
2 CONC s a Lawyer, First Class. I took a position as an assistant in the Ministry of Internal Affairs. Later on, on January 17, 1871, I was appointed to my present position in charge of legal affairs (HERREDFOGED) in East and West Hou Pa
2 CONC rishes.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 1, 1860, I was married to ABELONE SØNDERGAARD.
2 CONT
2 CONT At Skorpinggaard, November 28, 1888
2 CONT
2 CONT M. KJELDSEN " " "
2 CONT
2 CONT This additional data has been assembled on Michael Kjeldsen after the time of the submission of the above translated document.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1902, MICHAEL KJELDSEN asked to be relieved of his position in East and West Hou Parishes and was given his release on September 20 of the same year. In 188 he was made a KNIGHT OF DANNEBROG and in 1901 was made a DANNEBROGSMAN
2 CONC . As of 1907, MICHAEL and ABELONE were living in Aarhus, Denmark.
