1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "THE FAURSCHOU FAMILY"  "FAVR" = "Bountiful"  "SKOV" = "Forest"  "FAVRSKOV" = "Bountiful Forest"  Although the name "Faurschou" originally appeared around 1277 as "Farscogh", it had  evolved into "Farskov" by the e
2 CONC arly 18th Century when we pick up the ﬁrst identiﬁed  ancestor of the "FAURSCHOU" family. A literal translation of its parts show that the  name "FAURSCHOU" means, literally, "Bountiful Forest".  The founding ancestor of the FAURS
2 CONC CHOU family was CHRISTIAN SØRENSEN  FAURSCHOU. He was a supervisor and custodian of the FAVRSKOV farms in Lyngaa  Parish in the Sabro District of Denmark around 1760.  He was born in 1737 in Aarhus, Denmark. In Sabro District, he 
2 CONC was known as "The Little  Count", in 1769 he married Mette Johanne Rasmusdatter (Lassen). She was born in  1747 and dies June 16, 1822. She was the daughter of a free-hold farmer from  Brendstrup Overgaard in Tilst Parish by the n
2 CONC ame of Rasmus Andersen Lassen.  Rasmus Andersen Lassen was born in 1715, christened in Tilst Church on November 3,  17??, and died in 1776. He was buried on January 6th. Mette Johanne's mother was  Apollone Sørendatter who was bor
2 CONC n in 1718 on the Søndergaard Farm in Laasby  Parish. Apollone died in Brendstrup Overgaard. Apollone's parents were Søren  Pedersen and Anna Mortensdatter.  Christian Sørensen FAURSCHOU, along with his partner, Frederik Christian 
2 CONC DAHL, took  over the debts of a certain Jacob BREGENDAHL who owned the grain works (mill) at  Aarhus when he decided to declare his bankruptcy in 1790.  At oublic auction, Christian Sørensen bought the Aarhus acreage, stables, min
2 CONC e and  windmill as well as the manastery meadow and four other pieces of land. He paid  15,480 Risgbanksdaler for all of this property.  In 1793, Christian Sørensen FAURSCHOU withdrew from his partnership with DAHL. At  this point
2 CONC  in time, the mill's value had increased to 10,000 Rigsbanksdaler. (In the period  from 1790 to January 1, 1792, when they took over the mill, the mill alone was worth  only 2,006 Rigsbanksdaler, 3 marks ans 12 skillings of which 
2 CONC the monastery properties  accounted for only 500 Rigsbanksdaler of this amount.)  (A public loan, obtained through the inﬂuence of a secret banker -- a certain Mr. Hoegh  Guldberg -- in 1790 helped Christian Sørensen FAURSCHOU and
2 CONC  his partner DAHL to  purchase the mill and monastery properties.  During the Napoleonic wars, Christian Sørensen became a horsetrader and seller in  Tilden. He was a good businessman and was lucky enough to be the best trader in 
2 CONC the  area. He became a very prosperous man. He also owned, on his own, some other lands  and properties around Aarhus, together with continued ownership of the four ﬁelds  behind the monastery.  Just two months after his wife's de
2 CONC ath, Christian Sørensen followed her to his grave. He  died in Aarhus on August 28, 1822 at the age of 85 years and was buried in the "south"  cemetary where the present day Aarhus City Hall stands on Parkalle (Park Avenue).  Chri
2 CONC stian Sørensen and Mette Johanne had eleven children in all: seven sons and four  daughters. Eight of these (5 sons and 3 daughters) survived into adulthood and raised  families of their own. It is from these eight children that a
2 CONC ll "FAURSCHOUS" are  descended. At the time of Christian Sørensen's death, three sons and two daughters  had preceded him to their graves.  Christian Sørensen's net worth at the time of his death was as follows: 5,488  Rigsbanksda
2 CONC ler (Rbdlr), 2 Marks (Mk.) and 11 Skillings (Sk.) tihs amount was in silver. In  currency, he left 7,557 Rbdlrs. 2 Mks, (in terms of 1987 currency this would be  aproximately 1,500,000 Kroner) He left each of his surviving sons 78
2 CONC 4 Rbdlrs, 6 1/7 Sks  in Silver and 1,079 Rbdlrs, 3Mks, and 13 5/7 Sks in currency. To each of his remaining  daughters, he left 392 Rbdlrs, 3 1/4 Sks. in silver and 539 Rbdlrs, 3Mks. and 6/7 Sks. in  curreny.  Abelone FAURSCHOU (#
2 CONC 2) and Anders FAURSCHOU (#6) had reached adulthood but  had died before Christian Sørensen had changed his will so their shares were divided  among each of their surviving children. Jens Lassen (#4) and Peder (#8) gave their  shar
2 CONC es of the estate to their brother Rasmus (#5) as he was the least well off of all the  surviving children.  During the era of the births of Christian Sørensen and Mette's children, baptismal and  burial records were often more acc
2 CONC urate and closely kept than birth and death records.  Accordingly, the following footnotes contain baptismal (and burial) dates for these  children and may be used to more accurately determine their lifespans  SUPPLEMENTAL DATA:  
2 CONC (A) An ofﬁcial census dated July 1, 1787 showed that Christian Sørensen and Mette  Johanne had their seven surviving children as of this date living with them. As of 1787,  the old custom of children's names being that of their fa
2 CONC ther's ﬁrst name plus "sen" for  sons and "datter' for daughters was in use and thus the children were listed in this  census as follows:  FAMILY MEMBERS 
2 CONT     * Søren CHRISTIANSEN <nowiki>-------------------</nowiki> 16 years old 
2 CONT     * Abelone CHRISTIANSDATTER <nowiki>-------</nowiki> 12 years old 
2 CONT     * Margrethe CHRISTIANSDATTER <nowiki>-----</nowiki> 9 years old 
2 CONT     * Jens Lassen CHRISTIANSEN <nowiki>-----------</nowiki> 8 years old 
2 CONT     * Rasmus CHRISTIANSEN <nowiki>-----------------</nowiki> 7 years old 
2 CONT     * Anders CHRISTIANSEN <nowiki>-----------------</nowiki> 5 years old 
2 CONT     * Ole CHRISTIANSEN <nowiki>-----------------------</nowiki> 3 years old  This census document also listed the following servants and boarders (tenants) as living  with Christian Sørensen and Mette Johanne at this time:  SERVAN
2 CONC TS: 
2 CONT     * Jens LADEFOGED (unmarried) <nowiki>------------</nowiki> 47 years old 
2 CONT     * Niels PEDERSEN (unmaried) <nowiki>---------------</nowiki> 57 years old 
2 CONT     * Anne NIELSDATTER (unmarried) <nowiki>--------</nowiki> 30 years old 
2 CONT     * Karen JENSDATTER (unmarried) <nowiki>---------</nowiki> 24 years old 
2 CONT     * Poul SCHMIDT (unmarried) <nowiki>----------------</nowiki> 49 years old  BOARDERS: 
2 CONT     * Jørgen FRYDENLUND (Butcher's assistant <nowiki>-----</nowiki> 40 years old 
2 CONT     * Johan KNUDSBERG ( from Copenhagen) <nowiki>--------</nowiki> 30 years old  At the time of this 1787 census, Christian Sørensen and his family were living at  Clostergade #14 in Aarhus, Denmark. The population count for Aarhu
2 CONC s in 1761was  4,156.  (B)  Another census document - this one dated February 1, 1801 - listed both Christian  Sørensen and Mette Johanne and their family members, servants and boarders living  together as of that date. By this dat
2 CONC e, the use of "FAURSCHOU" as the family name  was in use. This census lists the place of residence of Christian Sørensen and his  family as being behind the Aarhus convent number 149 which was known as  "Munkegade". As of this dat
2 CONC e, the population of Aarhus was 4,102 persons. Below are  listed the census results insofar as they concern Christian Sørensen and his household:  FAMILY MEMBERS: 
2 CONT     * Jens Lassen FAURSCHOU <nowiki>----------------------------</nowiki> 23 years old 
2 CONT     * Rasmus FAURSCHOU <nowiki>----------------------------------</nowiki> 21 years old 
2 CONT     * Peder FAURSCHOU <nowiki>-------------------------------------</nowiki> 10 years old 
2 CONT     * Margrethe FAURSCHOU <nowiki>-------------------------------</nowiki> 24 years old 
2 CONT     * Mette Johanne Kathrine LETH (granddaughter) -- 1/2 year old 
2 CONT ** Mette Johanne Kathrine LETH (#3A) was the daughter of Margrethe Leth (nee  Faurschou) and her husband, Peder.  SERVANTS: 
2 CONT     * Søren JENSEN <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> 47 years old 
2 CONT     * Karen Tuesen Nette <nowiki>-------------</nowiki> 27 years old  BOARDERS: 
2 CONT
